  "worked_solution": "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point where $x=3$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(3,2).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ at $(3,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(3,2) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{(3)^{2}-2(2)^{2}}}{2-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{9-8}}{-1} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
